Kilix is a terminal built on a fork of kitty, with a pixel desktop, pane
and tab control for coding agents, and a small app catalog.

Kilix installs as a per-user checkout that builds its own engine and keeps
itself up to date, so this port installs no Kilix files. It pulls in the
packages that checkout builds and runs against: the toolchain, the engine's
libraries, Pillow and Go, the desktop's Media Player and browser libraries,
and the Xvfb and python-xlib its X11 apps use. Then, as your user:

  git clone --recursive https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/kilix.git \
      ~/.local/gpu_terminal/sources/kilix
  ~/.local/gpu_terminal/sources/kilix/kilix --build
